-- title:
--   Lying over the Gauss ring: j(τ)-floor versus j(qτ)-floor
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and work inside the Laurent series field $L((T))$. Let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of $\mathtt{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb{Q}\ (\Gamma_H(q^2M'))$, where $H=\mathtt{levelH}\ q\ M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ and $\mathtt{qExpFunctionFieldC}$ denotes the field generated by the $q$-expansions of quotients $f/g$ of modular forms of equal weight having integral expansions; let $K_0$ be the corresponding field for $\Gamma_0(M')$, with $K_0\le K$. Assume the substitution $T\mapsto T^q$, given by [`ModularCurve.qExpand L q`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), maps $K_0$ into $K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$. Let $W_0\subseteq K$ and $O_0\subseteq K_0$ be the valuation subrings consisting of those $f$ with $f\cdot y=x$ for power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal (the Gauss rings). Then, for every valuation subring $B$ of $K$, the condition that $B$ contracts to $O_0$ along $K_0\hookrightarrow K$ holds if and only if, for every $w\in K$ of the form $w=\mathtt{qExpand}\ L\ q\ x$ with $x\in K_0$, one has $w\in B$ precisely when $w$ satisfies the same Gauss condition relative to $A$.
--
--   This is the comparison of the two $\Gamma_0(M')$-floors of the full-level field at $q$: a valuation subring of $K$ lies over the Gauss ring of the floor generated by $j(\tau)$ exactly when it lies over the Gauss ring of the floor obtained by the substitution $\tau\mapsto q\tau$, the hypothesis that the latter floor is contained in $K$ making the right-hand condition non-vacuous. It is used in the identification of valuation subrings fixed by the level automorphisms, via [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.algebraMap_mem_comap_gauss_iff_of_isLevelAutAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.algebraMap_mem_comap_gauss_iff_of_isLevelAutAt).
